course: dictionary
lesson: 7525
title: Words for people who do a job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A practitioner is a person who does a skilled job, especially a doctor, nurse or lawyer. «In the UK your first stop for most health problems is the GP, the general practitioner or family doctor.» GP is short for general practitioner, and the sentence tells you a GP is a family doctor. So a practitioner must be a skilled worker, here a doctor.
explain: The word can also mean a person who regularly does something. «A practitioner of yoga» is someone who does yoga often and knows how to do it well. Check by swapping in a simpler idea: «a person who does yoga regularly» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «A GP is a general practitioner, or family doctor, who looks after all kinds of health problems.» The clues are looks after and health problems, which tell you the practitioner is a person who helps sick people with their skills.
fact: A practitioner is a person who does a skilled job.
fact: «General practitioner» means a family doctor, and it is often shortened to GP.
fact: A «nurse practitioner» is a skilled nurse, and a «health practitioner» is a skilled worker in health care.
fact: A practitioner of something is a person who does it regularly, such as «a practitioner of yoga».
fact: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, read the sentence to see which meaning fits.
exercise: «A GP is a general practitioner, or family doctor, who looks after all kinds of health problems.» What is a practitioner? | A shop that sells medicine | A patient waiting in a queue | *A person who does a skilled job, like a doctor | A hospital bed
exercise: Priya says, «She is a practitioner of yoga.» What does this mean? | She is sick and needs a doctor | She is a teacher at a school | *She does yoga regularly and well | She owns a yoga mat
exercise: «In the UK your first stop for most health problems is the GP.» Which words in the sentence mean the same as GP? | *general practitioner or family doctor | health problems | most health | first stop
test: «The nurse practitioner checked my arm and said it was not broken.» What is a nurse practitioner? | A patient who is ill | *A nurse who is a skilled health worker | A person who sells nurses' uniforms | A nurse who does a skilled job
test: Mum says, «My sister is a practitioner in Canada.» What does practitioner most likely mean? | A child at school | *A person who does a skilled job | A place where people wait | A sort of car
exam: Which sentence uses practitioner to mean a person who regularly does something? | The doctor wrote a note | The GP saw me this morning | The hospital was busy | *He is a practitioner of martial arts, training every day
